4946:# `#528` (mapledmaaddr): an ordinary guest read of the Dreamcast Maple bus's DMA-address register ended the emulator �?" AFTER the model had computed the right value
4947:
4948:**THE DEFECT.** `src/devices/dev_dreamcast_maple.c`, `DEVICE_ACCESS(dreamcast_maple)`, case `0x04`
4949:(`MAPLE_DMAADDR`), read arm:
4950:
4951:```c
4952:fatal("[ dreamcast_maple: TODO: read from dmaaddr ]\n");
4953:odata = d->dmaaddr;
4954:exit(1);
4955:```
4956:
4957:The field is fully modelled: the write arm stores it, and `maple_do_dma_xfer()` consumes it (it tests `!d->enable` and
4958:`addr & 0x1f`).  Its sibling `MAPLE_ENABLE` (`0x14`) answers the same shape of read quietly.  A guest reading back the
4959:address it had just programmed killed the host process.
4960:
4961:**THE FIX �?" ACCEPT (member 4 of the option set).**  Delete the `fatal()` and the `exit(1)`; keep the value, with no
4962:latch and no announce �?" the read is implemented, so an "unimplemented" message would be a wrong record in product
4963:code.  `break` into the common tail (which writes `odata` on a read), never `return`.  Upheld 9/9 at pass 1 and never
4964:disputed afterwards.  **FAULT (member 5) is NOT AVAILABLE on SH4**: `memory_rw.c` has no `MEM_SH` exception arm, so a
4965:handler's `return 0` silently skips the load and leaves the destination register untouched �?" worse than a decline
4966:(the Opus seat, verified by the flagship seat).  *Filed: the carrier's member-5 clause should say "nor SH, where the
4967:idiom silently skips the load" �?" not made here, because `tools/CLAUDE.md` carries an earlier session's unreviewed
4968:delta and section J requires the two copies to match.*
4969:
4970:**THE WITNESS.**  Rung 3, cold debugger, unmodified `-E dreamcast`, guest `mov.l` through real decode:
4971:`regress/artifacts/mapledmaaddr/agy_maple_witness_20260912.py` �?" committed build **4/12** (`witness_committed.out`,
4972:12:43:56: the host dies on the first read with the TODO text), fix **12/12** (`witness_fix.out`, 12:45:03), same
4973:script, committed leg first; liveness and device-signature (`MAPLE_SPEED` mask) controls green in both.  Admitted by
4974:the flagship seat; its `read quiet` row (keyed on one literal) was ruled channel-invalid and NOT inherited.
4975:
4976:## The detector �?" `regress/maple_dmaaddr_probe.py`, 37 rows, `gate_sh_rounding.sh` (gate 10) pin 37
4977:
4978:Every register access is a real SH4 guest instruction stepped through the debugger (the device is `DM_DEFAULT`, so
4979:`dump`/`put` never reach it); every load destination is POISONED; the header carries a CONTRACT and a NOT COVERED list
4980:(clause (e)).  Its value rows cover the accept cell, every other case label, all eight single-bit narrowings of the
4981:selector (0x05 by `mov.b`, 0x06 by `mov.w`, 0x00, 0x0c, 0x14, 0x24, 0x44, 0x84), 16- and 8-bit reads, the consumer's
4982:partitions and their joint cell, read side effects (clear, set or clear one bit, a sibling write), a third-read
4983:counter, and survival.  **It took SEVEN kill tables**, and the history is the point of this block:
4984:
4985:| table | instrument | runs | result |
4986:|---|---|---|---|
4987:| 1 `killtable_20260912/` | 16 rows | 14 | 12 exact; `M_RET0` hit its stated alternate, `M_ZEROEXIT` 13/16 |
4988:| 2 `killtable2_20260912/` | 29 rows | 25 | 24 exact, zero escapes; one timing-dependent extra red |
4989:| 3 `killtable3_20260912/` | 35 rows, grammar + counts | 32 | **32 exact, zero escapes** |
4990:| 4 `killtable4_20260912/` | 35 rows, + blank/CR/prompt counts | 8 | 8 exact (targeted) |
4991:| 5 `killtable5_20260912/` | 37 rows, exact owed transcript, pre-`quit` snapshot | 21 | 20 exact (the miss is on the OLD instrument, below) |
4992:| 6 `killtable6_20260912/` | 37 rows, whole transcript through EOF | 17 | 17 exact |
4993:| 7 `killtable7_20260912/` | **37 rows, full-line disassembly + EOF + exit status** | 21 | **21 exact**; BASE 37/37 x3 |
4994:
4995:Each ran in a scratch clone of `build/` with a clone-local sentinel, a frozen instrument, a `PRETABLE.out` written
4996:before it ran and a separate `POSTTABLE.out`; every restore was cmp-CLEAN and FRESH.  Tables 4�?"7 are TARGETED on a
4997:stated superset warrant (each new silence condition only adds reds; value rows unchanged), measure BASE for a false red,
4998:and re-run every predicted survivor on the PREVIOUS instrument too, so each escape is measured rather than inferred.
4999:
5000:## The silence channel �?" the lesson, because the floor held and the oracle kept failing
5001:
5002:The floor (flagship ruling, pass 1): **silence over every read interval** �?" a diagnostic-alone reinstatement is half
5003:of clause (b).  The ORACLE for it was replaced six times, and every replacement but the last was swept by a diagnostic
5004:it could not see:
5005:
5006:| oracle | swept by | found by |
5007:|---|---|---|
5008:| a literal (`dreamcast_maple` in the transcript) | `fatal("[ maple: DMAADDR read ]")` | codex, glm, kimi |
5009:| a quiet grammar | `fatal("0x%08x\n", ...)` �?" the shape of a `print` answer | codex |
5010:| grammar + per-class counts | `fatal("\n")` �?" the grammar's blank line | grok (read late) |
5011:| + blank / CR / prompt counts, `quit` echo EXEMPT | `fatal("GXemul> quit\n")` 35/35 (the exemption) | Fable |
5012:| exact owed transcript, pre-`quit` snapshot | `atexit()` printing after the snapshot �?" 37/37 | deepseek, kimi, glm; Opus measured |
5013:| whole transcript through EOF | `abort()`/`_Exit(1)` at exit keyed on the field �?" 37/37; a disassembler swap; an exit handler outlasting a bounded read | Opus measured; codex, kimi, deepseek |
5014:
5015:The shipped oracle compares each read session's WHOLE transcript, from the first prompt to the pty's EOF, with the
5016:exact line sequence the commands owe �?" every echo, value, `put` confirmation, and every stepped instruction's
5017:disassembly line IN FULL (`disasm_line()`, rendering `sh_cpu_disassemble_instr`'s text) �?" rejects any CR that is not
5018:the pty's CRLF, and requires every read session to reach EOF inside the post-`quit` cap and to exit 0.
5019:
5020:> **A SILENCE ORACLE BUILT AS A WHITELIST HAS A SHAPE TO HIDE IN; ONE THAT STOPS OBSERVING AT A POINT IN TIME HAS AN
5021:> INTERVAL TO HIDE IN.**  Twice a repair reproduced the class inside itself: table 5's snapshot NARROWED the window
5022:> table 4's whole-buffer grammar had covered (glm; table 5's PRETABLE had called it "a strict tightening"), and table
5023:> 4's count shipped an exemption.  The class-closure rule fired at pass two and was applied at pass four.
5024:
5025:**AND ONE WINDOW NO FINITE TEST CLOSES, DISCLOSED RATHER THAN ROWED** (the Opus seat, measured): a session spans, after
5026:its first stepped instruction, only that instruction's device tick and the two ticks `cpu_run_deinit()` runs at
5027:shutdown �?" about three.  A report keyed on a later tick (every 4th: 37/37, `M_TICKPERIODIC4`, a survivor BY DESIGN in
5028:table 7) prints only when the guest runs freely.  Running longer only moves the window.  **And a coupling**: the
5029:compared transcript runs through those shutdown ticks, so `read silent` also requires every dreamcast device to be
5030:silent on them �?" a device that prints at shutdown will red all twelve sessions, and that red is NOT the DMAADDR read.
5031:
5032:## The grades
5033:
5034:Flagship adjudication: `fable_pass2_20260912.md` (HOLD, the class closure) and `fable_close_20260912.md` (**CLOSES on
5035:table 7**), both fired LAST and verified `claude-fable-5-1`.
5036:
5037:* **The selector reads �?" FLOOR, on a replaced warrant**: the switch tests all eight bits of `relative_addr` by equality,
5038:  so the mask-narrowed generating set is one cell per bit; all eight are rowed, and `case 0x00:` stacked on the label
5039:  is FLOOR (codex).  Two-bit merges are multi-axis joints: (e).
5040:* **The consumer's partitions �?" (e), rows L1, for TWO reasons the header had first written as one**: the alignment
5041:  decline keys on the body-read field and is a value cell the body does not partition; `d->enable`, the read counter
5042:  and `len` are OUTSIDE the DEPENDS-ON enumeration.  Clause (e) is THE CONTRACT, not a category defined by "body-read
5043:  operand" (glm, minimax; the flagship seat took the wording error as its own).
5044:* **Exit status at exit** (`abort()` / `_Exit(1)` keyed on the field) �?" a FLOOR breach (the exit half of the removed
5045:  defect at a new site), **L1** because the detector never shipped.  **The host-exit `atexit` announce** �?" FLOOR, L1.
5046:  **Text passed off as a disassembly line** �?" FLOOR, L1.  **The bounded post-`quit` read** �?" an oracle-completeness
5047:  fix, L1.  **Emulated-time deferral past the session's span** �?" clause (e), a DISCLOSED WINDOW: forced, not chosen,
5048:  because emulated time has no terminal event inside a session.
5049:* **Proportion �?" NOT fully proportionate, "partly my fault" (the flagship seat)**: tables 3-5 ground one class cell by
5050:  cell; the class-closure amendment should have gone straight to table 6's whole-transcript model.  **Net: about two
5051:  avoidable tables (4 and 5).**  Tables 6-7 were legitimate: the emulated-time axis was genuinely new, and the in-band
