19609:### `mapledmaaddr` -- SHIPPED as `#528` (2026-09-12); residuals FILED, none owed
19610:
19611:The fix (ACCEPT: delete the `fatal` + `exit(1)` around the `MAPLE_DMAADDR` read) and its 37-row detector shipped as
19612:`#528`, with `gate_sh_rounding.sh` (gate 10) pinned at 37.  The detector took SEVEN kill tables; the flagship
19613:adjudications (`regress/artifacts/mapledmaaddr/fable_pass2_20260912.md`, `fable_close_20260912.md`) ruled the grades
19614:and closed the chain on the silence oracle.  Filed, each disclosed in the probe's NOT COVERED list, NOT owed:
19615:
19616:* **A decline or exit KEYED on sibling state the rows leave at reset** -- `} else if (d->timeout) { ... } else {`
19617:  survives every read session (the timeout is 0 in all twelve).  One `MAPLE_SPEED` write before a read in any session
19618:  would pin the `timeout != 0` cell; not taken, because the arm's body reads no sibling field (clause (e)).
19619:* **An effect after the third read in one process** (counter > 3), **two-bit selector merges**, **high-bit masking**
19620:  (covered by the values, never separately measured), **environment-keyed effects**.
19621:* **Clause (c) was never a kill-table leg.**  The four control rows carry it by construction; the named measurement is
19622:  a binary built WITHOUT the maple device at 0x5f6c00, which must red `ctrl devsig maple`.  Cheap; not run.
19623:* **The carrier's member-5 clause** should gain "nor SH, where the idiom silently skips the load" (the flagship seat's
19624:  pass-1 ruling).  Not made: `tools/CLAUDE.md` carries an earlier session's unreviewed delta, and section J requires
19625:  the root and tools copies to match -- so it lands with whatever round reviews that delta.
19626:* **The dead-pty `quit` echo (table 2's one miss) is MOOT, not filed:** the shipped oracle reads the whole transcript
19627:  through EOF and requires exit 0 in every read session, so a dead session reds deterministically.
19628:* **The emulated-time window is DISCLOSED, not owed** (flagship ruling, `fable_close_20260912.md`): a session spans the
19629:  first-step device tick plus the two `cpu_run_deinit()` ticks, so a diagnostic keyed on a later tick (a periodic
19630:  summary; `M_TICKPERIODIC4` 37/37 in kill table 7, by design) is unobservable by any finite session.
19631:* **A no-DMAADDR silence-control session for the shutdown-tick coupling** (flagship seat, "worth filing; not owed"):
19632:  `read silent` runs through the two shutdown ticks, so it also requires every dreamcast device to be silent on them.
19633:  One session that runs `quit` WITHOUT reading DMAADDR and requires ITS transcript to be exact would make a future
19634:  shutdown print by another device red THAT row too -- distinguishing "another device speaking" from "the read
19635:  speaking".  Cost: one session; changes the row count and the gate pin.
19636:
19637:### `silencewhitelist` (LOW, harness) -- filed 2026-09-12 from `#528`
19638:
19639:`#528`'s silence row went through SEVEN oracles -- a literal, a quiet grammar, per-class counts, counts with an
19640:exemption, a pre-`quit` snapshot, a whole transcript with a bounded read and prefix-matched disassembly -- and each of
19641:the first six was swept by a diagnostic in a legal shape or a later interval (a token-free message, a bare hex line, a
19642:blank line, the exempted `quit` text, an `atexit` print, an exit-time crash, a swapped disassembler).  **A silence
19643:oracle built as a whitelist has, by construction, a shape to hide in -- and one that stops observing at a point in time
19644:has an interval to hide in.**  The closure is an EXACT OWED TRANSCRIPT computed from the commands (`owed()` /
19645:`disasm_line()` / `noise()` / `unclean()` in `regress/maple_dmaaddr_probe.py`): the whole session through the pty's
19646:EOF, every line in full, EOF and exit 0 required.  Other detectors in `regress/`
19647:carry silence rows keyed on a literal or a grammar; which of them are FLOOR-graded, and so owe the same closure, has not
19648:been censused.  **The deriver, not a list:** grep `regress/*_probe.py` for rows whose name or note says `silent` /
19649:`quiet` / `noise`, and read each oracle.  Not owed by any shipped round: each row's grade was ruled in its own round.
19650:
19651:### `pit8253flood` (MED) -- filed 2026-09-16 from `#530`'s closing pass 5, found while measuring something else
19652:
19653:**`dev_8253.c` has TWO GUEST-DRIVABLE `fatal()` ARMS WITH NO LATCH, and a previous round of this project put them
19654:there.**  An ordinary 16-bit MSB write to counter 1 or counter 2 reaches:
19655:
19656:```c
19657:	case 1:	fatal("TODO: DMA refresh?\n");
19658:		break;	/*  #223: (Codex/Fable) warn+ignore, don't exit() the host  */
19659:	case 2:	fatal("TODO: 8253 tone generation?\n");
19660:		break;
19661:```
19662:
19663:**`#223` did the de-fatalisation and did not bound what it left behind.**  Both arms used to end the process; both now
19664:announce, unconditionally, once per write.  `grep -cE 'static int|warned|\(once\)' src/devices/dev_8253.c` returns
19665:**ZERO** -- the file carries no latch of any kind.
19666:
19667:**MEASURED, not estimated:** the `#530` c5 measuring seat's 150-row 8253 prototype counts the emissions and prints the
19668:count -- **18 of each per session, 36 per run**.  It moves no row (the probe parses `print` output), which is why it is
19669:a filed item and not a `#530` finding.
19670:
19671:*** THIS IS THE CARRIER'S OWN STANDING RULE UNMET, AT A SITE THIS PROJECT CREATED. ***  *"A guest-drivable `fatal()`
19672:needs a latch and not a verbosity flag"* -- and the reason is measured elsewhere in the tree: `fatal()` has **no
19673:early-out at all** (`src/core/debugmsg.c`, the `fatal()` body against `debug()`'s `if ((quiet_mode && !ss) || v < 0)
19674:return;`), so `-q` cannot silence it.  The house idiom is **N = 1 per DEVICE INSTANCE plus an explicit `(once)`
19675:marker**, which is ~82% of all suppression markers in `src/devices/`.

